From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:12:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] LOCAL TEST ONLY: drm: apple: Register a DCP's Type-C
 routes in the order of their index

The route with index 0 is the pipeline's default PHY: dcp->phy before a
route is selected, and where a released Type-C-only pipeline parks
(typec_routes[0]). The physical ports, and with them the connector
numbers, follow the registration order too. Both came from the order of
the typec-routes children in the device tree, which so far is always the
index order.

A route added at run time by an OF changeset is attached as the first
child of typec-routes. The T8122 display gate's front-port route
(route@1, next patch) would then become the dcpext's default PHY and
DP-1. Collect the available routes by their reg first (a missing,
out-of-range or repeated index refuses the probe, as a missing or invalid
one did) and register them in index order. Nothing changes for a device
tree whose routes are already in order.

